@startuml
title Messenger - Simplified Group Message Sequence
hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
skinparam maxMessageSize 230
skinparam ParticipantPadding 20
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F3FC

participant "Sender Browser" as Sender
participant "Messenger Server" as Server
database "D1\nMessenger Data" as Data
participant "Other Group Members\n(open browser sessions)" as Recipients

note over Sender, Recipients
  Local application on one computer. D1 is a combined logical store.
  Main requirements: FR-06, FR-14, FR-15, FR-17, NFR-03.
end note

Sender -> Server : Send group message\n(session, group ID, text)
Server -> Data : Get sender identity from session\nand current group membership
Data --> Server : Login and membership information

alt Not logged in OR not a current group member
  Server --> Sender : Reject: login required or access denied
  note over Server, Data : Do not store or distribute the message.
else Logged in AND a current group member
  Server -> Data : Store message with authenticated\nsender ID and group ID
  Data --> Server : Accepted message record
  Server --> Sender : Own message for display
  Server -> Data : Get other active sessions\nand current members for this group
  Data --> Server : Authorized recipient information
  Server -> Recipients : Message for authorized open sessions only
  Recipients -> Recipients : Display sender and message text
end

note over Server, Recipients
  Recipient filtering also checks login and current membership.
  Other users and former members receive no group content.
  Delivery transport and repeated requests are omitted at this level.
end note

note over Sender, Recipients
  Accepted does not mean read. Offline delivery is unresolved (IA03 Q-03).
  Timing and reliability targets still require testing.
end note
@enduml
